# shotcraft — local environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is committed and
# must never hold a real value. Read by `platform/_env.py`, which is applied by
# every entry point via `--origin` and friends.
#
#     copy .env.example .env      # Windows
#
# Nothing in this repository *requires* a secret today. Every upstream fetch is
# public: `platform/mirror_site.py` pulls the deployed site and the GitHub
# release assets without authentication. The variables below are grouped by
# whether something reads them, because an empty list of "just in case" entries
# is how a config file starts lying about what a project needs.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the origin
# THE one variable that changes what the site emits. Every canonical link,
# og:url, sitemap entry and JSON-LD `url` is generated from it, and there are
# 480 + 471 of those. It is currently hardcoded to `https://shotcraft.example`,
# which is a placeholder: if that string reaches production the site's own
# metadata tells a crawler the pages live somewhere they do not.
#
# Read by: platform/site/build_site.py, platform/site/seo.py
SITE_ORIGIN=https://shotcraft.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- machine paths
# Already supported, already optional. Listed here so one file holds every knob.
#
# `CINEMATIQUE_DIR` — where the MIT-licensed catalog source is cloned.
#   platform/catalog/layer_gate.py. Default: C:\susa ai\cinematique
CINEMATIQUE_DIR=C:\susa ai\cinematique

# `CHROME_PATH` — absolute path to Chrome, when it is not on PATH.
#   platform/site/selftest.py runs the site in a real browser.
# CHROME_PATH=C:\Program Files\Google\Chrome\Application\chrome.exe

# `BASE` — point the API selftest at an already-running server instead of
# letting it start one. platform/api/selftest.py
# BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- deploy
# Unused by any current code path; present because deployment is the next step
# and a secret should be created once, in one place, rather than improvised at
# the moment of a first deploy.
#
# Cloudflare Pages deploy token. Scope: Account > Workers Scripts > Edit.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# GitHub token. Only needed to raise the API rate limit for
# `platform/mirror_site.py --media`, which downloads 214 release assets (128 MB).
# A fine-grained token with read-only public_repo scope is enough; without one
# the download works but is anonymous and slower.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- agents
# Neither is read by the build. Present only if you intend to run agent or LLM
# steps over this corpus from your own scripts — the index, the wiki and the
# briefs are all generated deterministically and need no model today.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- never commit
# A guard, not a setting. `platform/doctor.py` fails if any of these appear in a
# tracked file, because the failure mode is a key in git history rather than a
# key in a working copy, and git history does not take a `--delete` well.
#
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, GITHUB_TOKEN, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY